{"actions":[{"date":"2026-06-02","source":"Senate","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the Committee on Veterans' Affairs.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"The title of the measure was amended. Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 216 - 201 (Roll no. 190). (text: CR H3684-3685)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 216 - 201 (Roll no. 190). (text: CR H3684-3685)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"On motion to recommit Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 208 - 210 (Roll no. 189).","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H3710-3711)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"POSTPONED PROCEEDINGS - At the conclusion of debate on H.R. 1041, the Chair put the question on motion to recommit and by voice vote, announced the ayes had prevailed. Mr. Bost demanded the yeas and nays and the Chair postponed further proceedings until a time to be announced.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question on the motion to recommit was ordered pursuant to clause 2(b) of rule XIX.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Ms. Morrison moved to recommit to the Committee on Veterans' Affairs. (CR H3692)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H.R. 1041.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1041, H.R. 6047 and H.R. 1329. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 1041, H.R. 6047, and H.R. 1329 under a closed rule. The resolution provides for one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 1300. (consideration: CR H3684-3692)","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2026-05-19","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 1300 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 1041, H.R. 6047 and H.R. 1329. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 1041, H.R. 6047, and H.R. 1329 under a closed rule. The resolution provides for one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit on each bill.","type":"Floor"},{"date":"2025-06-05","source":"House floor actions","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 112.","type":"Calendars"},{"date":"2025-06-05","source":"House floor actions","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Veterans' Affairs. H. Rept. 119-143.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-06-05","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Veterans' Affairs. H. Rept. 119-143.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-05-06","source":"House committee actions","text":"Ordered to be Reported by the Yeas and Nays: 13 - 11.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-05-06","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-02-06","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Veterans' Affairs.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-02-06","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-02-06","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[{"action":"On agreeing to the Rules amendment (A001) Agreed to without objection.","amends":null,"chamber":"House of Representatives","date":"2026-05-21","id":"hamdt-221","label":"H.Amdt. 221","purpose":"Pursuant to H. Res. 1300, the amendment in the nature of a substitute recommended by the Committee on Veterans Affairs now printed in the bill is considered as adopted.","sponsor":{"bioguide_id":null,"name":null,"party":null,"state":null},"status":"Agreed to","submitted":"2026-05-21","url":"https://www.congress.gov/amendment/119th-congress/house-amendment/221"}],"total":1},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2026-06-02","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"Senate","code":"ssva00","name":"Veterans' Affairs Committee","subcommittees":[]},{"activities":[{"date":"2026-05-21","name":"Unknown"},{"date":"2026-05-21","name":"Unknown"},{"date":"2025-06-05","name":"Reported By"},{"date":"2025-05-06","name":"Markup By"},{"date":"2025-02-06","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsvr00","name":"Veterans' Affairs Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":70,"fetched_at":"2026-10-26T06:55:08+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-26","importance":40,"viability":68.5}],"id":"119-hr-1041","importance":40,"importance_band":"limited","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":39.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Affects VA beneficiaries who have appointed fiduciaries to manage their benefits, as well as the VA and the Department of Justice firearms background check system.","evidence":"prohibits the VA from transmitting personally identifying information of a veteran or a beneficiary to the NICS solely on the basis that such veteran or beneficiary has an appointed fiduciary","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":50},{"assessment":"Alters background check reporting practices for affected veterans, preventing automatic disqualification or reporting based solely on fiduciary status.","evidence":"The Secretary may not transmit... personally identifiable information of a beneficiary, solely on the basis of a determination by the Secretary to pay benefits to a fiduciary","evidence_verified":false,"key":"magnitude","score":40},{"assessment":"No federal fiscal appropriations or economic impacts are stated in the source.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":10},{"assessment":"Amends Title 38 of the United States Code to restrict information sharing between the VA and the Department of Justice and requires an agency notification.","evidence":"Chapter 55 of title 38, United States Code, is amended by inserting after section 5501A the following new section","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":35},{"assessment":"Imposes permanent restrictions on VA information transmittal and requires a one-time notification to the Attorney General within 30 days.","evidence":"The Secretary shall, within 30 days of the enactment of the Veterans 2nd Amendment Protection Act... notify the Attorney General","evidence_verified":false,"key":"duration","score":60}],"missing_information":["Exact number of veterans currently reported to NICS under the existing standard is not provided.","Specific administrative costs for compliance are not estimated."],"rationale":"The bill restricts the Department of Veterans Affairs from transmitting beneficiary personally identifying information to NICS solely because a fiduciary is appointed, unless there is a judicial finding of danger.","score":40},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-26T06:58:56+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr1041/BILLS-119hr1041rfs.htm"]},"introduced_date":"2025-02-06","is_demo":false,"label":"H.R. 1041","latest_action":{"date":"2026-06-02","text":"Received in the Senate and Read twice and referred to the